WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.481
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, so there’s
this brand new show my friends at Geek and

00:00:03.481 --> 00:00:06.240
Sundry are doing that I’m really excited
about.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.450
So I’m going to be doing a few bonus videos
for it.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.210
It’s called Arcade Arms and they’re going
to be forging real life versions of famous

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.600
video game weapons and doing some cool stuff
with them.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.150
Mostly smashing things, I think their permit
for human testing is still pending.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.710
So this video is going to be a breakdown of
some of the weapons they’re going to be

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:25.630
using and when they’re going to start posting
episodes.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:29.740
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
I’ll have links for the show down in the

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:30.740
description.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.759
So the show is actually going to be hosted
by Nika Harper.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.350
If you haven’t seen her before she’s been
doing a lot of stuff with Geek and Sundry

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.499
for the past couple of years like Wordplay.

00:00:37.499 --> 00:00:41.870
She also did a League of Legends show on their
official channel called Summoner Showcase.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:42.890
I think she’s really good.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.670
I really like her enthusiasm for breaking
stuff with giant weapons.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.050
Because all these weapons are based on really
big video games they also did a bunch of cool

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.660
interviews with the people that actually made
the games.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.850
So like for instance, in the first episode
they have the Lead Loremaster for Elder Scrolls

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.420
on talk about the story behind the weapon
they make in that video.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.170
So really a big part of all this is doing
the lore for each of the weapons, then actually

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.170
making them in real life.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.170
They went all the way to Canada to find the
person to make their first one.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.530
Here are the top 5 things I’m most excited
about.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.430
Number 5 - learning about how they make each
of the weapons.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.840
The smiths that they picked to make everything
talk a lot about the practical aspects of

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:22.720
the weapons and why they have specific features.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.149
Number 4 - The locations.

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:27.280
They actually had to travel a lot to shoot
the show.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:33.659
Most of the people that make the weapons are
specialists and live all over the place.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:39.289
They had to go to Canada for the first episode.

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:41.670
Number 3 - The lore behind the weapons.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:45.490
If you’ve seen some of my other videos you
know I like to research mythology a lot.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.430
They talk to a lot of the people at each of
the game companies about the stories behind

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:50.430
the weapons.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:54.399
It’s like learning about Game of Thrones
from George RR Martin.

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:58.979
Number 2 - Cool behind the scenes info about
each of the games.

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:02.979
In addition to talking about the weapons in
the games, they get a lot of cool behind the

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:06.429
scenes details about why the game designers
made certain story choices.

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:11.770
You’d be surprised at the amount of time
developers devote to the story aspects of

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:12.770
games.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:20.130
and Number 1 - Watching them actually use
the weapons.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:24.330
They went to a lot of LARP societies to learn
about how say a giant mace would be used in

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:28.410
a real battle and why you’d choose that
weapon instead of say, a sword.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.580
They take it one step further too and smash
the hell out of stuff.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:37.280
The mace they made is like 35 pounds, which
is more than enough to crush someone’s skull

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.050
even if they’re wearing plate armor.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:46.951
So here’s what the episodes are going to
be, they’re all going to post on Geek And

00:02:46.951 --> 00:02:48.370
Sundry’s main channel once every two weeks.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.790
The first one will be Molag Bal’s Mace from
Elder Scrolls Online.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:52.790
That will air next week.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:53.790
May 13th.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.280
Then two weeks after that will be the Gael
Bolg from Final Fantasy Realm Reborn and the

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.620
third one will be Zelda’s Hero Bow from
Legend Of Zelda.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.980
That will air June 10th.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:11.750
So remember new episodes every two weeks.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:16.650
For my bonus videos I’m going to talk a
little bit about the characters and the lore

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.590
behind the mythology behind the weapons and
the games.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:25.060
So let’s talk some Elder Scrolls Online.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:29.090
In case you haven’t been playing the beta,
Elder Scrolls Online is a brand new MMO based

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:31.800
on Bethesda’s Elder Scrolls mythology like
Skyrim.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.140
So think Skyrim MMO.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:39.110
It’s been out on PC since April but it’s
coming to Xbox One and PS4 later this year

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.640
if you’re a console gamer.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.010
The Weapon they’re doing for the first Episode
belongs to Molag Bal, so let’s break him

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.010
down.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:53.400
He’s one of the sixteen daedric prince end
bosses in the Skyrim Dragonborn DLC.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.190
He was appeared in Oblivion.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:59.940
But for the purposes of this video we’ll
just stick to The mmo.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:06.870
The Daedric Princes are like the most powerful
of the Gods and each of them has their own

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.260
separate plane of existence.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:13.530
In the game all of them are associated with
super weapons you can obtain, like the mace.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:18.160
They’re like raid quality items with mega
bonuses.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.489
Molag is mostly like a harvester of souls.

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:25.630
Part of the quest you have to complete to
get his mace involves convincing someone to

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:30.770
sacrifice their soul to him.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:36.650
So it’s one of those alignment quests that
takes you down a much darker road.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:44.250
But if you like playing evil characters it’s
a lot of fun.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.250
Quick side note.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.930
One of the first games that gave you a lot
of freedom with your alignment and quest choices

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:53.410
was the first Knights of The Old Republic.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:56.730
Playing Revan as evil always led to way better
cut scenes.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:02.330
Because the character is part of the new MMO
they got Malcolm McDowell to do the voice.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:03.790
Which is really freaking awesome.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:06.270
He plays some of the best evil video game
characters.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:13.470
The Mace itself has a lot of vampiric bonuses
and you can upgrade it, but you need to max

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.470
out blacksmithing to do it.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.040
The funny thing about equipping it is that
it’s so big it takes up most of the screen.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.600
So it’s just really hard to see what’s
going on when you’re playing.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.830
Molag Bal is the main villain of the MMO,
future expansions will probably add in lore

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.550
from the other Daedric princes.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.180
The interesting thing about the story of the
MMO is that it incorporates player resurrection

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.320
as part of the conceit of the game.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.540
Molag Bal has basically stolen your soul so
you keep getting resurrected.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:38.120
As you play through the game you try to get
it back.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.880
I guess so you can finally die.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.780
There are three playable factions right now
and nine different races.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:47.770
So there’s a little more choice for people
who are getting burnt out on Warcraft.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:52.470
Plus no matter which class you choose, DPS,
Melee or Caster you can still tweak for armor

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.470
and weapon skills.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:57.940
So you can be a caster that wears plate.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:03.220
The only bummer is that because of the era
the game takes place in, there aren’t any

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.220
dragons.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:05.600
But they’ll probably be incorporated in
a future expansion.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:11.170
So I’ll be doing a couple more bonus videos
for each of the weapons and games they do.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.780
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.980
And links for the actual show are in the description.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:20.190
The first episode premieres next week on Tuesday
on Geek and Sundry’s youtube channel.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:25.530
